A||N||3||Rumor||Annoying Buzzing Sound||||1||
Z||000000||Rumor||11-27-2001||03:17 AM||||Hi!<BR>I'm a Fiero Newbie. I just got a 85 GT V6 Auto. Every time I turn the key(but don't try to start it), I hear a buzz for two seconds or so, and then it stops.  If I start the car, the buzzing stays on.(it almost sounds like the motor that is in the AC system)  It fluctuates higher or lower whenever I push the power window switches or the brake pedal. It sounds like it is coming from somewhere in the center console.  It isn't coming from a speaker.   Have you ever heard of this?  I have already removed the center console, and haven't found the source of this annoying buzz-whine yet. Thanks for all of your help so far!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||RossT||11-27-2001||03:27 AM||||Welcome to the forum!!<P>Your fuel pump is making that buzzing sound.<BR>More than likely the previous owner replace the pump with a non AC-Delco pump.  Or it could be that your pump is going out.  The formula that I just purchased had the same problem.  The fuel pump was only a few weeks old.  The previous owner put in a Carter fuel pump.  I droped the tank and put in an AC Declo, now its as silent as it should be.<P>It could also be that your fuel filter is partially pluged.  I would start there first.<P><BR>You will find that the fiero works best with<BR>GM or Ac-Delco parts.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||11-27-2001||06:37 AM||||I didn't make that noise.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Try cutting off the power to the fuel pump and then try the key 'on'.  Mine made the same sound before it quit.  <P>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000003||Rumor||11-27-2001||10:20 AM||||THANKS! I read somewhere that when you turn the key, it makes the fuel pump go for a sec or two.  I will check out the fuel filer and the pump, and let you know how it goes.<P>Now, I can drive my Fiero without having to blast the stereo to drown out the buzzzzzzz...<BR>||||reg||1
